<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<FBType Name="Q_LockUnlockMask" Comment="Command Lock/UnlockMask( Part 6 - F.46 )">
	<Identification Standard="ISO 11783-6" Description="Copyright (c) 2022 HR Agrartechnik GmbH  &#10; &#10;This program and the accompanying materials are made  &#10;available under the terms of the Eclipse Public License 2.0  &#10;which is available at https://www.eclipse.org/legal/epl-2.0/  &#10; &#10;SPDX-License-Identifier: EPL-2.0  &#10;   &#10;   &#10;see Description Tab">
	</Identification>
	<VersionInfo Organization="HR Agrartechnik GmbH" Version="1.0" Author="Franz Höpfinger" Date="2022-07-08">
	</VersionInfo>
	<CompilerInfo packageName="isobus::UT::Q">
		<Import declaration="isobus::UT::Q::const::IDs::ID_NULL"/>
	</CompilerInfo>
	<InterfaceList>
		<EventInputs>
			<Event Name="INIT" Type="EInit" Comment="Service Initialization">
				<With Var="QI"/>
				<With Var="u16MaskId"/>
			</Event>
			<Event Name="REQ" Type="Event" Comment="Service Request">
				<With Var="QI"/>
				<With Var="u8LockCmd"/>
				<With Var="u16LockTimeoutMs"/>
			</Event>
		</EventInputs>
		<EventOutputs>
			<Event Name="INITO" Type="EInit" Comment="Initialization Confirm">
				<With Var="QO"/>
			</Event>
			<Event Name="CNF" Type="Event" Comment="Confirmation of Requested Service">
				<With Var="QO"/>
				<With Var="STATUS"/>
				<With Var="s16result"/>
				<With Var="u8OldLockCmd"/>
				<With Var="u16OldLockTimeoutMs"/>
			</Event>
		</EventOutputs>
		<InputVars>
			<VarDeclaration Name="QI" Type="BOOL" Comment="Quality Input - TRUE to enable service" InitialValue="TRUE"/>
			<VarDeclaration Name="u16MaskId" Type="UINT" Comment="Object ID of data mask or user layout data mask to lock or unlock " InitialValue="ID_NULL"/>
			<VarDeclaration Name="u8LockCmd" Type="USINT" Comment="0 = Unlock, 1 = Lock data mask or user-layout data mask"/>
			<VarDeclaration Name="u16LockTimeoutMs" Type="UINT" Comment="Lock timeout in ms or zero for no timeout "/>
		</InputVars>
		<OutputVars>
			<VarDeclaration Name="QO" Type="BOOL" Comment="Quality Output - TRUE if service executed successfully"/>
			<VarDeclaration Name="STATUS" Type="STRING" Comment="Service Status"/>
			<VarDeclaration Name="u8OldLockCmd" Type="USINT" Comment="Old 0 = Unlock, 1 = Lock data mask or user-layout data mask"/>
			<VarDeclaration Name="u16OldLockTimeoutMs" Type="UINT" Comment="Old lock timeout in ms or zero for no timeout "/>
			<VarDeclaration Name="s16result" Type="INT" Comment="retval see description"/>
		</OutputVars>
	</InterfaceList>
	<Attribute Name="Documentation" Type="CDATA"><![CDATA[<h1>Command Lock/UnlockMask( Part 6 - F.46 )</h1>

<p>This message is available in VT Version 4 and later.
This command is used by a Working Set to disallow or allow screen refreshes at the VT for the visible Data Mask or User-Layout Data Mask owned by the requesting Working Set.</p>

<h2>Valid values for u16MaskId (the mask to lock or unlock)</h2>

<p>A mask Object ID is valid if it falls within one of the following ISO 11783-6 ID ranges (Annex F.46):</p>
<ul>
	<li><strong>DataMask</strong>: 1000 – 1999</li>
	<li><strong>WindowMask (User-Layout Data Mask)</strong>: 34000 – 34999</li>
</ul>

<p>ID_NULL (65535) is not a valid command target — the command fails with a response code (the mask to lock/unlock must match the currently visible mask).</p>

<h2>param[in] {state, uint8_t}</h2>

<p>0 = Unlock, 1 = Lock data mask or user-layout data mask</p>

<h2>param[in] {objectID,  uint16_t}</h2>

<p>Object ID of data mask or user layout data mask to lock or unlock</p>

<h2>param[in] {timeout_ms,  uint16_t}</h2>

<p>Lock timeout in ms or zero for no timeout</p>

<h2>Return Values (s16result):</h2>

<h3>int16_t</h3>

<ul>
	<li><span style="color:#27ae60">VT_E_NO_ERR (0)</span> - OK</li>
	<li><span style="color:#e74c3c">VT_E_NOT_READY (-131)</span> - VT client not yet ready</li>
	<li><span style="color:#e74c3c">VT_E_OVERFLOW (-6)</span> - buffer overflow</li>
	<li><span style="color:#e74c3c">VT_E_NOACT (-8)</span> - Command not possible in current state</li>
	<li><span style="color:#e74c3c">VT_E_NO_INSTANCE (-21)</span> - No VT client available</li>
	<li><span style="color:#e74c3c">VT_E_ISO_INSTANCE_INVALID (-129)</span> - Identifier for instance (connection) invalid</li>
	<li><span style="color:#e74c3c">VT_E_NOT_ALIVE (-130)</span> - Identifier for instance valid, but VT Dead.</li>
	<li><span style="color:#2980b9">VT_OK_BUFFERED (18)</span> - command buffered, waiting for VT to be ready</li>
</ul>
<h2>Instanz-Eindeutigkeit (Instance Uniqueness)</h2>

<p>Dieser Baustein erfordert Instanz-Eindeutigkeit bezüglich <strong>u16MaskId</strong>. Es darf im gesamten Programm nur eine Instanz von <code>Q_LockUnlockMask</code> für dieselbe Masken-ID existieren. <code>u16MaskId</code> wird bei <code>INIT</code> eingelesen — eine zweite Instanz auf dieselbe Masken-ID wird bei <code>INIT</code> deaktiviert (STATUS = "This objID is already in use").</p>
]]></Attribute>
	<Attribute Name="eclipse4diac::core::TypeHash" Value="''"/>
</FBType>
